## 4. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — Split Model Shard Resolution

**Responsibilities:** Resolves the shard paths of a split GGUF model from any shard's filename, validates that all shards exist, and returns them in split order.

**Proposed change:** Add a `gguf_split_count()` function that extracts the shard count from a filename without opening files, and add a `gguf_split_no()` that extracts the shard number. These allow callers to validate shard completeness before attempting to open all files.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -18,6 +18,30 @@
 namespace strata {

+/// Extracts (shard_no, total_count) from a split filename, or (0,0) if not a split name.
+inline std::pair<int,int> gguf_split_parse(const std::string& path) {
+    static const char tag[] = "-of-";
+    const size_t at = path.rfind(tag);
+    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || path[at - 6] != '-' || path.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 ||
+        path.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
+        return {0, 0};
+    int no = 0, n = 0;
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
+        const char a = path[at - 5 + i], b = path[at + 4 + i];
+        if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9') return {0, 0};
+        no = no * 10 + (a - '0');
+        n = n * 10 + (b - '0');
+    }
+    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {0, 0};
+    return {no, n};
+}
+
+inline int gguf_split_count(const std::string& path) { return gguf_split_parse(path).second; }
+inline int gguf_split_no(const std::string& path) { return gguf_split_parse(path).first; }
+
 // Split models: `<name>-00001-of-0000N.gguf` ... `<name>-0000N-of-0000N.gguf`, as llama.cpp's gguf-split names
```

**Verification cases:**
1. Call `gguf_split_count("model-00002-of-00004.gguf")` and assert it returns 4; call `gguf_split_no` and assert it returns 2.
2. Call `gguf_split_count("model.gguf")` and assert it returns 0 (not a split name); call `gguf_split_parse("model-00005-of-00004.gguf")` and assert it returns `{0,0}` (no > n).

